    <string name="tasks_trigger_help_calendar">Runs before an entry in your phone\'s calendar starts. Locus reads the calendar every 15 minutes and plans a run for the right time; Android can hold it back a few minutes while the phone is idle.</string>
    <string name="tasks_trigger_help_ntfy">Runs when a message arrives on an ntfy topic. Anything that can send a web request can post to one (a server, a script, a webhook), on ntfy.sh or your own server. Locus checks every 15 minutes, or later while the phone is idle; it keeps no connection open.</string>
    <string name="tasks_trigger_help_mail">Runs when mail arrives in the agent\'s own mailbox (forward or filter mail to it). Locus looks for new mail every 15 minutes, or later while the phone is idle, reading only the sender and subject.</string>
    <string name="tasks_trigger_help_app">Runs when another app (Tasker, Automate, a script) sends Locus the event below. It arrives at once; Locus\'s automation settings and the list below decide who may send it.</string>
